SUMMARY:Application Deadline: Wake County Nonprofit Institute
DESCRIPTION:Applications are now open for the second class of the Wake County Non-Profit Institute from Wake County Public Health in collaboration with the Wake County Office of Organizational Excellence. \nIs your organization looking to strengthen its sustainability and build long-term capacity? If so\, this institute is designed for you. \nOver the course of four months\, participants will: \n\nAttend four 90-minute sessions\, with at least one representative from your organization participating in person.\nCollaborate with up to 19 other nonprofit organizations and learn from one another’s experiences and best practices.\nReceive a one-year membership to the North Carolina Center for Nonprofits upon successful completion of the program.\nReceive five hours of additional consulting after completing the sessions to help implement what you’ve learned.\n\nThere is a participation fee of $100. The application deadline is July 23. \nLearn more about the program at an upcoming informational session: \n\nJuly 7th\, 1pm-2:30pm\nJuly 10th\, 10am-11:30am\nJuly 14th\, 2pm-3pm\n\nLearn more and apply here.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/application-deadline-wake-county-nonprofit-institute/
LOCATION:Virtual
END:VEVENT
