SUMMARY:Training: Mental Health Begins by Birth
DESCRIPTION:Join the ARCh Project for a virtual workshop series on July 31st and August 7th\, 9:30am-12:30pm ET. The workshop series will build understanding of infant and early childhood mental health\, discuss the impact of traumatic experiences on early development\, and consider how you can make a difference in a young child’s life. This training is for anyone in NC whose professional work supports the relational\, emotional\, and mental health of babies and young children. \nWorkshops will be in English with Spanish simultaneous interpretation. \nRegister here. \nPlease contact mary.wise@duke.edu with any questions.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/training-mental-health-begins-by-birth/
LOCATION:Zoom
END:VEVENT
