SUMMARY:Adult Mental Health First Aid for ECE Professionals
DESCRIPTION:Early Care and Education (ECE) professionals are invited to join Alliance Health and the ITTI Care Project for a free Adult Mental Health First Aid (MHFA) training on August 14th. MHFA is a nationally-recognized course that teaches you how to identify\, understand\, and respond to signs of mental illnesses and substance use disorders. Participants will gain practical skills to provide initial support to someone who may be experiencing a mental health or substance use crisis. \nDate: Friday\, August 14th \nTime: 9am-5pm \nLocation: 2024 W Main St.\, Durham\, NC 27705 \nRegister here by July 15. \n 
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/adult-mental-health-first-aid-for-ece-professionals/
LOCATION:Erwin Square Mill Building\, 2024 W Main St\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
END:VEVENT
