SUMMARY:Training: Culturally Responsive Ethical Decision-Making
DESCRIPTION:Join El Futuro for this free 3-hour training on culturally responsive ethical decision-making on September 11 from 12-3pm. \nStandard ethical training often focuses strictly on risk management\, leaving providers ill-equipped when professional codes clash with the cultural realities of their clients. This interactive 3-hour training moves beyond “what to do when you have a dilemma” by examining ethics as a proactive\, culturally grounded practice. \nDrawing from current literature on transcultural ethical decision-making\, this session will assist providers in deconstructing standard Western ethical assumptions (e.g. rigid boundaries\, hyper-individualism) and evaluating how these assumptions can inadvertently harm Latine clients. Participants will explore common ethical friction points—such as dual relationships and confidentiality—through the lens of core Latine values like personalismo\, familismo\, and respeto. Finally\, attendees will learn and apply a structured\, transcultural decision-making matrix to complex case scenarios\, ensuring their ethical choices are both professionally sound and culturally affirming. \nNBCC and ASWB continuing education credit will be offered. \nRegister here.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/training-culturally-responsive-ethical-decision-making/
LOCATION:Zoom
END:VEVENT
