SUMMARY:NC Infant and Early Childhood Mental Health Association: 2026 Conference
DESCRIPTION:Registration is now open for NCIMHA’s annual conference\, Hand in Hand: Promoting Early Relational Health. Come together to learn about infant and early childhood mental health (IECMH)\, two-generational approaches\, and maternal mental health. Join NCIMHA for 3 days of learning\, camaraderie and connection. Similar to IECMH\, two-gen approaches and maternal mental health\, Early Relational Health is the state of emotional well-being that grows from the mutual\, positive connections between babies\, toddlers\, and their caregivers. \nOctober 8-9: Two full in-person days at Cape Fear Community College in Wilmington\, NC \nOctober 15: One full day of virtual sessions \nThe total cost for participation is $175 for NCIMHA members\, $225 for non-members\, and $100 for students. Participants unable to join in person may choose to register for the 1-day virtual event for $75. Scholarships are available. Four sessions – two in the morning and two in the afternoon – will bring together local and national voices in infant and maternal mental health spaces. \nLearn more and register here: North Carolina Infant Mental Health Association Annual Conference
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/nc-infant-and-early-childhood-mental-health-association-2026-conference/
LOCATION:Cape Fear Community College\, 411 N Front Street\, Wilmington\, NC\, 28401\, United States
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR